In article <1991Feb26.165555.18589@watcgl.waterloo.edu> hrdoucet@watcgl.waterloo.edu (Heloise Doucet) writes:
>I am running NetHack 3.0 on the Mac(Samurai) and I am having a few problems.
>
>1) I am wearing armor - Dwarven Mithril Coat - it is not cursed and I can't
>take it off. When I give the Remove Armor command and get a list of my
>armor items, it is not there. Is this a bug or is it something I did?

Naw.  It probably means you're wearing a cloak over it.  Take off the
cloak first.

>2) When I sacrifice monsters on my altar, nothing happens or it says that
>I feel inadequate. When I pray I lose levels. I do not kill monsters that
>do not attack me. I don't sacrifice anything in particular - anything that
>wanders by. Also, I have got my katana from my God. Help!

Gods are strange creatures.  They can get mad for no particular
reason.  Once they're mad, they're very hard to appease.  Bothering
them too often can be annoying.

If you're going to sacrifice, it should be some edible monster.  The
bigger and nastier, the better.  Rotten corpses are not accepted.
Small ones may be accepted but have no effect.

>3) In my intrinsics it says that I aggravate monsters. Is there something
>that you eat that will cause this? I am not wearing anything (such as a ring)
>that specifically aggravates monsters. Could it be anything I am wearing or
>carrying? 

Eating a human or a dog or a cat will do this.  Also, some critters
can cast a spell to do this.  

